          "final_text_tail": "All 614 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\nSummary of changes:\n\n**`src/click/core.py`**:\n- Added `cleanup_timeout: float | None = None` parameter to `Context.__init__`\n- Validation: raises `ValueError` if `cleanup_timeout` is zero or negative\n- Inherits `cleanup_timeout` from parent context when not explicitly set\n- Added `cleanup_timeout` attribute to `Context`\n- Updated `close()` to run cleanup in a daemon thread when a timeout is set, using `threading.Thread.join(timeout)`. If the worker is still alive after the timeout, logs a warning and abandons the cleanup (graceful degradation). If the worker finished with an error, re-raises it.\n- `_make_sub_context` now propagates `cleanup_timeout` to sub-contexts\n- Updated docstrings\n\n**`src/click/shell_completion.py`**:\n- `_resolve_context` sets `cleanup_timeout=10.0` via `ctx_args.setdefault(...)` so shell completion resilient-parsing contexts respect a timeout during cleanup",
